"Some keyboard layouts (such as AZERTY) require a modifier to press a number key. This causes problems for switching to a window, tab, or split pane by pressing modifier+number: you might need other modifiers or conflicting modifiers. When “Emulate US Keyboard” is enabled, you can press the configured modifier plus the key on the top row that corresponds to a number key on a US keyboard. For example, on AZERTY, the & key would act as the 1 key." = "某些键盘布局（如 AZERTY）需要修饰键才能按下数字键。这会导致通过按修饰键+数字来切换窗口、标签页或分屏时出现问题：您可能需要其他修饰键或存在冲突的修饰键。启用“模拟 US 键盘”后，您可以按配置的修饰键加上顶行中对应 US 键盘数字键的按键。例如，在 AZERTY 布局上，& 键将充当 1 键。";
"The leader behaves like a modifier key, such as Command or Option, but is a separate keystroke. It can be used in key bindings. For example, if you set the leader to ⌘b then you could bind an action to the two-keystroke sequence “⌘b x”. ⌘b is the recommended leader and that keystroke will not be used for other purposes in the future." = "Leader 键的作用类似修饰键（如 Command 或 Option），但它是一个独立的按键。它可用于键绑定。例如，如果您将 Leader 设为 ⌘b，则可以将操作绑定到双键序列“⌘b x”。⌘b 是推荐的 Leader 键，该按键未来不会用于其他用途。";
